          "role": "function",
          "content": "<document>\n<title>List of continents and continental subregions by population</title>\n<content>\nPopulation ranking of the world's continents and continental subregions\n\nThis is a list of continents and continental subregions by population.\n\n\n\n\n## Distribution of populations by the United Nations geoscheme\n\n[edit]\n\n\nWorld population by continent, 2021\n\n1. Asia (59.4%)\n2. Africa (17.6%)\n3. Europe (9.40%)\n4. North America (7.50%)\n5. South America (5.50%)\n6. Oceania (0.60%)\n7. Antarctica (0.00%)\n\n\n\n\n| Continent | Population(2021)[1][2][3] | % of world | \u00b1% p.a.2010\u20132013\n |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **World** | 7,909,295,151 | 100% | 1.17%\n |\n| Asia | 4,694,576,167 | 59.4% | 1.04%\n |\n| Africa | 1,393,676,444 | 17.6% | 2.57%\n |\n| Europe | 745,173,774 | 9.4% | 0.08%\n |\n| North America | 595,783,465 | 7.5% | 0.96%\n |\n| South America | 434,254,119 | 5.5% | 1.04%\n |\n| Oceania | 44,491,724 | 0.6% | 1.47%\n |\n| Antarctica | 3,000 | 0% | N/A\n |\n\n\n\n\n| UN Subregion | Population(2021)[1][2] | % of world | \u00b1% p.a.2010\u20132013\n |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **World** | 7,909,295,151 | 100% | 1.17%\n |\n| Southern Asia[a] | 1,989,452,478 | 25.2% | 1.32%\n |\n| Eastern Asia | 1,663,696,923 | 21.0% | 0.57%\n |\n| Southeast Asia | 675,796,065 | 8.5% | 1.20%\n |\n| Eastern Africa[b] | 461,141,845 | 5.8% | 2.89%\n |\n| South America | 434,254,119 | 5.5% | 1.06%\n |\n| Western Africa[c] | 418,544,337 | 5.3% | 2.78%\n |\n| Northern America | 375,278,947 | 4.7% | 0.85%\n |\n| Eastern Europe[d] | 291,464,162 | 3.7% | 0.23%\n |\n| Western Asia[e] | 289,733,123 | 3.7% | 1.98%\n |\n| Northern Africa[f] | 255,737,736 | 3.2% | 1.70%\n |\n| Western Europe[g] | 195,381,649 | 2.5% | 0.25%\n |\n| Middle Africa[h] | 190,267,973 | 2.4% | 2.79%\n |\n| Central America[i] | 177,661,929 | 2.2% | 1.40%\n |\n| Southern Europe | 152,130,606 | 1.9% | 0.24%\n |\n| Northern Europe[j] | 106,197,357 | 1.3% | 0.54%\n |\n| Central Asia | 75,897,577 | 1.0% | 1.43%\n |\n| Southern Africa | 67,984,554 | 0.9% | 0.91%\n |\n| Caribbean | 44,182,048 | 0.6% | 0.71%\n |\n| Australia and New Zealand | 31,050,816 | 0.4% | N/A\n |\n| Melanesia[k] | 12,188,834 | 0.2% | N/A\n |\n| Polynesia | 717,467 | 0.009% | N/A\n |\n| Micronesia | 534,606 | 0.007% | N/A\n |\n| Antarctica | 3,000 | 0% | N/A\n |\n\n\n1. **^** The UN geoscheme includes Afghanistan and Iran in Southern Asia.\n2. **^** The UN geoscheme includes the British Indian Ocean Territory, the Comoros, the French Southern Territories, Madagascar, Malawi, Mauritius, Mayotte, Mozambique, R\u00e9union, Zambia, and Zimbabwe in Eastern Africa.\n3. **^** The UN geoscheme includes Saint Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha in Western Africa.\n4. **^** The UN geoscheme includes Bulgaria, Czechia, Hungary, Poland, Romania, and Slovakia, as well as Siberia (Northern Asia) in Eastern Europe.\n5. **^** The UN geoscheme includes the South Caucasian countries of Armenia, Azerbaijan, and Georgia, as well as Cyprus and Turkey in Western Asia.\n6. **^** The UN geoscheme includes Western Sahara in Northern Africa.\n7. **^** The UN geoscheme includes the DACH countries and Liechtenstein in Western Europe.\n8. **^** The UN geoscheme includes Angola in Middle Africa.\n9. **^** The UN geoscheme includes Mexico in Central America.\n10. **^** The UN geoscheme includes the Baltic states, the British Isles, and the Channel Islands in Northern Europe.\n11. **^** The UN geoscheme includes Papua New Guinea in Melanesia.\n\n## Global, continental, and subregional totals from 1950 to 2021\n\n[edit]\n\nSee also: United Nations geoscheme\n\n### Africa\n\n[edit]\n\nEastern Africa| Year | Pop. | \u00b1% p.a. |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1950  | 66,923,000 | \u2014\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 |\n| 1960  | 84,305,000 | +2.34% |\n| 1970  | 110,428,000 | +2.74% |\n| 1980  | 147,512,000 | +2.94% |\n| 1990  | 198,232,000 | +3.00% |\n| 2000  | 259,373,000 | +2.72% |\n| 2010  | 342,743,000 |